bcm2835-codec: expose JPEG quality on the video ENCODE role

V4L2_CID_JPEG_COMPRESSION_QUALITY was only registered for the ENCODE_IMAGE
role (the still-JPEG node, /dev/video31), so continuous MJPEG produced by the
video ENCODE role (/dev/video11, V4L2_PIX_FMT_MJPEG -> MMAL_ENCODING_MJPEG) had
no quality knob and ran at the VideoCore firmware default. Register the same
control on the ENCODE role. The existing s_ctrl handler already maps it to
MMAL_PARAMETER_JPEG_Q_FACTOR on the output port, which the firmware honours for
MJPEG and ignores for H264, so this is safe for both output formats.

Signed-off-by: webcampi <webcampi@localhost>

--- a/drivers/staging/vc04_services/bcm2835-codec/bcm2835-v4l2-codec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/vc04_services/bcm2835-codec/bcm2835-v4l2-codec.c
@@ -3427,7 +3427,7 @@
 	case ENCODE:
 	{
 		/* Encode controls */
-		v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(hdl, 13);
+		v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(hdl, 14);
 
 		v4l2_ctrl_new_std_menu(hdl, &bcm2835_codec_ctrl_ops,
 				       V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_BITRATE_MODE,
@@ -3495,6 +3495,16 @@
 		ctx->gop_size = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, &bcm2835_codec_ctrl_ops,
 						  V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_GOP_SIZE,
 						  0, 0x7FFFFFFF, 1, 60);
+		/*
+		 * MJPEG (V4L2_PIX_FMT_MJPEG) shares the video ENCODE component, so
+		 * expose the JPEG quality control here too. s_ctrl already maps it to
+		 * MMAL_PARAMETER_JPEG_Q_FACTOR on the output port; the firmware honours
+		 * it for MJPEG and ignores it for H264. Without this the ENCODE node
+		 * ran MJPEG at the firmware default quality with no way to change it.
+		 */
+		v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, &bcm2835_codec_ctrl_ops,
+				  V4L2_CID_JPEG_COMPRESSION_QUALITY,
+				  1, 100, 1, 80);
 		if (hdl->error) {
 			rc = hdl->error;
 			goto free_ctrl_handler;
